      "side": 1,
      "message": "One potential option to save some more space would be to just have one `std::array\u003cDynamicOffset, kMaxDynamicOffsetsPerBindGroup\u003e`, and then have `PerBindGroup\u003cstd::pair\u003csize_t, size_t\u003e\u003e mDynamicOffsetRanges` that indexes into the array? Then we can return splices of the array when calling `GetDynamicOffsets()`. I think the downside of that is that you would need to do some more tracking, and also, when bind groups are overridden, probably need to make sure that the indices aren\u0027t changed (not sure if that\u0027s valid?)",
